{"duration_api_ms":185601,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bb57450a-c5b2-4e1b-81bd-718cab1cb581","total_cost_usd":1.2041091999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":50,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60420,"cache_read_input_tokens":1826946,"output_tokens":17758,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2697},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60420,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1291,"cache_read_input_tokens":92490,"cache_creation_input_tokens":268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":268},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":50,"outputTokens":17758,"cacheReadInputTokens":1826946,"cacheCreationInputTokens":60420,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2041091999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2697,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":60420,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":25,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"PKT-0131 is done and committed (`b6513c2`). Converting the 10-page Word document to PDF takes **1200 ms** at p50 (min 1083, max 1251, over 9 runs), and **98% of that is x2t**. All four acceptance commands pass, and `theseus scope-check` reports no changes outside the target.\n\n**What I built**\n- `.theseus/oracle/journeys/convert-docx-pdf.sh` and `convert-docx-pdf-run.cjs` play the integrator calling the API:\n  1. POST a signed request to `/ConvertService.ashx` (`async:true`, docx → pdf), pointing at `open-docx-10p.docx`, served from a local URL.\n  2. Re-post every 20 ms until the server says the conversion is finished.\n  3. Download the PDF to the last byte.\n  - Stage times come from the server's own debug logs, matched by the request key.\n- The existing `serve-integrated.sh` (from PKT-0126) is reused unchanged.\n- The map is `.theseus/journeys/convert-docx-pdf.md`. The stages add up to 1209 ms against the 1200 ms total (0.75% apart), with 0 ms unattributed.\n\n**Where the time goes**\n- **Server plumbing** (HTTP, token check, queue, fetching the source, storage, response) is about 15 ms in total.\n- **Polling** adds about 19 ms, which is the 20 ms poll interval I chose.\n- **x2t** is 1174 ms. Running x2t on its own on the same file splits it into:\n  - about 75 ms to start the process and read the docx;\n  - about 390 ms of fixed start-up (the JavaScript engine plus the bundled editor code), paid even for an empty document;\n  - about 585 ms to lay out the 10 pages and draw the PDF.\n\n**Decisions**\n- No browser: the user of this journey is an integrator calling the API.\n- Async mode with 20 ms polling. The server's sync mode only re-checks about once a second, so it would add up to ~1 s; the map notes this.\n- I used the same 10-page sample as the open journeys so the numbers can be compared.\n- There was no earlier map of this journey, so the comparison is with `baseline.md`: 767 ms there for a small template, where x2t was 70–90% of the time.\n\n**Problem found: x2t does not run the integrated code**\n- x2t loads a precompiled snapshot, `sdkjs/word/sdk-all.bin`. `serve-integrated.sh` replaces the JavaScript files but leaves this snapshot from the original package.\n- So every x2t run uses the packaged editor code, not the forks' branch. This also affects the save journey (PKT-0130).\n- I tested moving the snapshot aside: x2t rebuilt it on the next run and then took about the same time. I put the original back, byte-identical.\n- I couldn't fix the script here because it is outside this packet's target. I recorded a follow-up request at `.theseus/spawn/PKT-0131-serve-integrated-make-x2t-run-the-integrated-sdk.md`, priority high, which needs the `documentserver` environment.\n\nThe Executor log and the friction line are written. No command was refused.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- The fastest gain for conversion is a renderer that stays running, which would save roughly 0.45 s on every conversion. The rest is sdkjs word's layout and PDF drawing, which is shared with opening a document.\n- The next x2t diagnosis needs to cover all three x2t sub-steps. x2t has no internal timing log, so the split had to be inferred from standalone runs and strace.\n- Any overlay of the sdkjs code must also handle `sdk-all.bin`, or x2t keeps running the old code.","ttft_ms":3856,"type":"result","duration_ms":283797,"uuid":"b164ac68-7bc8-4037-8cb5-8948bacc7a88","ttft_stream_ms":2655,"time_to_request_ms":307,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":210,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":37,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":134,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":209,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":243,"process_anon_mib_result":153,"process_peak_rss_mib":278,"process_cpu_ms